# Stage 6 right clamp (D-075 visibility rule; game-design.md Stage 6
# "Difficulty and reach rules"): the solver route with RIGHT added from
# frame 560 on to every frame that doesn't hold LEFT (on the steamer the
# solver already drifts to the clamp; RIGHT there would walk her off its
# bow), so through the scroll Resi's hitbox stays at the right clamp (its
# left edge 242 px right of the camera from ~600) until her death at
# 3951. Measured on this replay (first frame any part of the enemy's
# hitbox is on screen -> first frame it reaches the clamp line, where she
# can be touched): swans #1-#3 63 frames (they trigger as soon as they are
# fully on screen, 20 frames in, hiss 32, then charge; the sprite shows ~5
# frames before the hitbox), Gelsen #1-#3 81-82 frames (60 frames hovering
# fully on screen, then the hunt), regatta boats #1-#2 85 frames (fully on
# screen ~30 frames in, then the 60-frame start). Swans and Gelsen never
# touch her (she dives under the swans and outswims the Gelsen as the
# solver does); she is in the air over regatta #2 as it passes (~3823),
# and regatta #3, which she meets at the surface while holding RIGHT,
# hits her at 3951, 86 frames after it first showed: the only death, by
# an enemy in view for > 60 frames.
